But we need candidate_prepared OA true. To get candidate_prepared we need to attach task profile and confirm preparedness. However load_origin_payload precondition requires candidate_prepared ?origin_availability (true). So we must have candidate_prepared before loading. So steps: attach_task_profile OA RTP, confirm_candidate_preparedness OA RTP, then load_origin_payload, then unload_origin_payload.

But attach_task_profile requires vehicle_allocated OA true (we have), candidate_created OA true (yes), route_task_profile_available RTP (we have). After attaching, route_task_profile_available becomes false. Then confirm_candidate_preparedness requires candidate_prepared false (we will have after attach? Actually confirm_candidate_preparedness precondition: candidate_created ?candidate, vehicle_allocated ?candidate, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, not candidate_prepared ?candidate. So after attach, we have candidate_task_profile_linked true, candidate_prepared false (still). So we can run confirm_candidate_preparedness, which sets candidate_prepared true and does not affect other things.

Thus after confirm_candidate_preparedness, OA is prepared.

Now we need to load/unload payload.

Load_origin_payload precondition: candidate_prepared OA true, origin_availability_node_linked OA ON true, cargo_available CPA true, not origin_availability_locked OA (currently false). So we can load.

After load: origin_node_occupied true, origin_availability_locked true, origin_payload_linked OA CPA true, cargo_available false.

Then unload_origin_payload precondition: candidate_prepared OA true, candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTP? Wait unload_origin_payload precondition includes candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile. Yes it requires candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTP (we have after attach). Also destination? Actually it's origin_availability version: unload_origin_payload parameters: (?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?route_task_profile - route_task_profile ?payload_unit - cargo_payload). Precondition includes candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile. So we need the task profile linked (we have). Also origin_availability_node_linked OA ON true, origin_node_occupied true, origin_payload_linked OA CPA true, not origin_availability_confirmed OA (currently false). So we can unload.

After unload: origin_node_ready true, origin_availability_confirmed true, cargo_available true, not origin_payload_linked OA CPA.

Thus after these steps we have origin_node_occupied true, origin_node_ready true, origin_availability_locked true, origin_availability_confirmed true, cargo_available true, candidate_prepared OA true, candidate_task_profile_linked OA RTP true, vehicle_allocated OA true (still), candidate_vehicle_linked OA VUA true (still). Good.

