Now we need to ensure transport leg assembled and loading authorized.

Transport leg assembly requires origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked, origin_availability_node_linked, destination_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready/destination_ready conditions depending on which assemble action we use. Since we want both origin_leg_loaded and destination_leg_loaded? Not required but we can use assemble_transport_leg which requires origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready (both ready) and origin_availability_confirmed and destination_availability_confirmed. However we will have origin_node_ready true after unload_origin_payload, and destination_node_ready true after unload_destination_payload. Also we need origin_availability_confirmed true (we will have after unload_origin_payload) and destination_availability_confirmed true (after unload_destination_payload). Also we need origin_availability_locked true and destination_availability_locked true (we will have after load_*_payload before unload? Actually after load_origin_payload we have locked true, after unload_origin_payload locked remains true. Similarly for destination. So after unload both, we will have locked true for both.

Thus we can use assemble_transport_leg after both origin and destination have been loaded and unloaded (so they are locked and confirmed, nodes ready and occupied). Let's verify preconditions for assemble_transport_leg:

(:action assemble_transport_leg
    :parameters (?origin_availability - origin_candidate_availability ?destination_availability - destination_candidate_availability ?origin_node - origin_node ?destination_node - destination_node ?transport_leg - transport_leg)
    :precondition
      (and
        (origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability)
        (destination_availability_locked ?destination_availability)
        (origin_availability_node_linked ?origin_availability ?origin_node)
        (destination_availability_node_linked ?destination_availability ?destination_node)
        (origin_node_ready ?origin_node)
        (destination_node_ready ?destination_node)
        (origin_availability_confirmed ?origin_availability)
        (destination_availability_confirmed ?destination_availability)
        (transport_leg_available ?transport_leg)
      )
    :effect
      (and
        (transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg)
        (transport_leg_origin_linked ?transport_leg ?origin_node)
        (transport_leg_destination_linked ?transport_leg ?destination_node)
        (not
          (transport_leg_available ?transport_leg)
      )
    )

Thus we need origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready true (we will have after unload). Also origin_availability_confirmed and destination_availability_confirmed true (after unload). Also origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked true (after load, still true after unload). So we can assemble after both unloads.

Now we need transport_leg_loading_authorized true. Action authorize_transport_leg_loading precondition: transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg, origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, not transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg.

Thus we need origin_availability_locked true (we have), candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha ?route_task_profile (we will have after attaching task profile to OA). Also transport_leg_assembled true (after assemble). So we can authorize after assemble.

Thus order: after we have OA and DA prepared (including load/unload to get locked/confirmed/nodes ready/occupied), we assemble transport leg, then authorize loading, then mark OA and DA dispatch_ready, then execute origin dispatch (to get dispatched OA and free VUA). Then we need to allocate dispatch slot to DA (if not already allocated) and make it dispatch_ready (we will have done mark after authorize). Actually we need to allocate dispatch slot to DA before we can mark it dispatch_ready? mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready does not require dispatch_allocated; it only requires destination_availability_locked, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready. So we can mark DA dispatch_ready before allocating dispatch slot? However goal requires dispatch_allocated DA true. So we need to allocate dispatch slot to DA after we have made it dispatch_ready? Actually allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate requires dispatch_ready ?candidate (the candidate). So we need DA to be dispatch_ready before allocating slot. So order: make DA dispatch_ready (via mark), then allocate dispatch slot to DA, then we have dispatch_allocated DA true and dispatch_ready DA true (still). However after allocating slot, dispatch_slot_available becomes false (but we don't need it). The goal does not require dispatch_slot_available.

Now we also need to allocate dispatch slot to OA and make OA dispatch_ready, then execute origin dispatch. However allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate requires dispatch_ready ?candidate. So we need OA dispatch_ready before allocating slot. So we need to mark OA dispatch_ready first, then allocate slot, then execute origin dispatch.

Thus overall sequence:

- Prepare OA (attach TP, confirm preparedness, load/unload payload) -> OA prepared, locked, confirmed, nodes ready/occupied, cargo available.
