_locked ?origin_availability) (origin_availability_confirmed ?origin_availability) (transport_leg_assembled ?transport_leg) (transport_leg_loading_authorized ?transport_leg) (not (dispatch_ready ?origin_availability)). No mention of candidate_task_profile_linked. So OA does not need task profile linked for dispatch ready. However confirm_candidate_preparedness required candidate_task_profile_linked. After we have confirmed preparedness, we may not need the task profile link anymore. So we can detach after confirmation. Good.

Thus we can attach task profile to OA, confirm preparedness, then detach task profile from OA (making route_task_profile_available again). Then attach to DA, confirm preparedness for DA, then we can keep DA's task profile linked for later steps (load/unload destination, mark destination dispatch ready, etc). Does DA need task profile linked for load_destination_payload? No, load_destination_payload precondition does not require task profile linked. It requires candidate_prepared, destination_availability_node_linked, cargo_available, not destination_availability_locked. So not needed. For unload_destination_payload precondition includes candidate_task_profile_linked ?destination_availability ?route_task_profile. So DA needs task profile linked for unload. Also mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready precondition includes transport_leg_assembled etc, but not task profile linked. However we might need task profile linked for something else? Not needed. However we might want to keep it for completeness but not required. However we need candidate_task_profile_linked destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha as a goal. So we must keep it linked at the end. So we should not detach from DA.

Thus plan: attach TP to OA, confirm preparedness OA, detach TP from OA (makes TP available), attach TP to DA, confirm preparedness DA (now DA has TP linked). Good.

Now we need to allocate vehicle units:

